-to/tools-classic/overview"}],"logprobs":[],"text":"**Foundry Agent Service** (Microsoft Foundry / Azure) is a **managed platform for building, deploying, and scaling AI agents**—i.e., AI apps that don’t just chat, but can **use tools, access data, and take multi-step actions** to complete tasks. ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/agents/overview))\n\n### What it provides (high level)\n- **Responses API (single entry point):** One API surface to run agents and access Foundry models plus platform tools (for example file search, code interpreter, memory, web search, and MCP servers). ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/agents/overview))  \n- **Agent Runtime:** Managed hosting that handles conversations/threads, tool calling, scaling, identity, and lifecycle management. ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/agents/overview))  \n- **Built-in tools:** Tools to ground responses on data and trigger actions/workflows (including web search/grounding, file/data search, and integrations like MCP). ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/agents/overview))  \n- **Model flexibility:** Use models from the Foundry model catalog and swap models without rewriting the whole app. ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/agents/overview))  \n- **Observability & security:** Tracing/metrics plus Microsoft Entra identity and RBAC options. ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/agents/overview))  \n\n### Agent types (how you can build)\n- **Prompt agents:** You define instructions (prompt-based) in the portal/SDK and Foundry runs it—minimal infra/code to manage. ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/agents/overview))  \n- **Hosted agents:** You bring code (using frameworks like LangGraph or an agents SDK), package as a container, and Foundry runs it behind a managed endpoint. ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry/agents/overview))  \n\n### Note about “classic” agents\nMicrosoft distinguishes **Foundry (classic) agents** from the newer Agent Service experience; **classic agents are deprecated and scheduled to retire on March 31, 2027**, with guidance to migrate to the newer Agents Service. ([learn.microsoft.com](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry-classic/agents/how-to/tools-classic/overview))  \n\n### Quick clarifying question\nWhen you say “Foundry Agent Service,” do you mean the **new Microsoft Foundry Agents Service** (Agents + Responses API), or are you currently using **Foundry (classic)** and looking for migration guidance?"},"sequence_number":127}

